WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.635
-It's been such a delight
this holiday week

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.670
to have our old friend
Fred Armisen

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.005
back with us on the drums.

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:09.108
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.010
You know, we've been
close friends for a long time.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.511
And, sadly, you know,

00:00:12.511 --> 00:00:14.514
we connect the most
when we see each other at work

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.182
because it allows us
this time to talk.

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:18.618
And as we go into
the holiday season,

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.119
I heard you backstage
saying to people --

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.355
because obviously every family

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.756
has different
holiday traditions.

00:00:23.756 --> 00:00:26.258
We wake up first thing Christmas
morning, we unwrap presents.

00:00:26.258 --> 00:00:28.728
But I heard you have
a non-present

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.863
Christmas morning
holiday tradition.

00:00:30.863 --> 00:00:32.164
-Yeah, this goes back to,
you know,

00:00:32.164 --> 00:00:34.100
when I was a kid
with my family and stuff,

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.736
and we used to just go out
and, you know, as a group...

00:00:37.736 --> 00:00:38.938
-As a family?
-...as a family

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:39.839
to New York City.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.007
And what we would do is like...

00:00:41.007 --> 00:00:43.709
we would just point
to, you know --

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.144
Like, if there was
a Santa Claus or something,

00:00:45.144 --> 00:00:48.214
we would just point
to the Santa Claus on the corner

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:49.782
and just sort of just
stand there for a while,

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:51.951
just kind of like...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.286
And then we'd move on..

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.187
So, like, we'd go by the tree
and we'd find, you know,

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:57.022
one of the tourists there
and just like, point to them,

00:00:57.022 --> 00:00:58.824
and...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.824 --> 00:01:00.260
-Oh, so you wouldn't --
It wasn't

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.660
just that you pointed at Santas.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:02.996
You would just point
at different things

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:03.963
over the course of the day?

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.664
-Yeah, just like in the morning.

00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:08.067
It was kind of like festive
because, you know,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:10.469
it was like a festive
feeling around it, and...

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:12.838
-Now, a lot of people
think pointing is rude.

00:01:12.838 --> 00:01:15.108
Do you, uh,
do you buy into that?

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.509
-I don't buy into that at all.
-Yeah.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.644
-Uh, I find it not rude.

00:01:18.644 --> 00:01:20.379
And the way we did it was
very sort of Christmassy.

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:21.548
Like...

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.582
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:25.418
You know?
-So I'm a tourist.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.053
Just hypothetically,
I'm a tourist,

00:01:27.053 --> 00:01:28.420
and I'm going
about myself, and I --

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.656
and how many of there
are in your group?

00:01:30.656 --> 00:01:31.924
-Four. So there's four of us.

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:34.360
-So I turn, and then I see
a family of four...

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:35.495
-Yeah.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.897
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:39.899
-And do you say --
do you say anything?

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.067
-No, because then, like,

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.568
throughout the rest
of the Christmas Day,

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:44.403
we sort of move on
to another family

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:47.106
or, like, to just workers.
-What's the longest

00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:48.908
you sort of silently pointed
at someone?

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:50.243
-Like a minute.
-Yeah.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.811
-Yeah.
-That's a long time.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.179
-You know, it is
once you're doing it.

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.714
And when you're a kid,
you know, you were a baby,

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:58.351
so it's, like, hard to hold,
you know, hold your...

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.553
-Oh, so the hard part
wasn't how awkward it was.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.054
It was just keeping your arm up.

00:02:02.054 --> 00:02:03.890
-You'd be surprised. Yeah.
-That's really --

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.225
-But as you get older,
as a teen, you know,

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:06.259
there's, like,
more energy behind it.

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.494
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:09.596 --> 00:02:11.931
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.002
-Merry Christmas, buddy.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.403
-Merry Christmas.

